  "final_span": "tilted or rotated or folded out of the way to provide more cargo carrying space.\nThere isn't any shortage of space for the driver and their passenger, but the rear seating area is quite cramped.\nSkoda Yeti goes for an off-roading feel\nThe boot stands out for its cube design, marked by noticeable patterns on the carpet, with a variety of small storage choices, and enough space in two full-size, divided seats to accommodate a wheelchair.\nInstead of incorporating the latest technology, Skoda opted for buttons and dials in the Yeti. This is likely to suit many buyers, though personal music players and Blackberrys may not be usable through Bluetooth or by plugging them in.\nThere is plenty of passenger ergonomics - you\u2019ll struggle to find much fault as to the Yeti\u2019s interior, particularly with the B&O sound system displaying good quality bass",
